foundation.question_text:
A network with source $S$ and sink $T$ is shown.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{decorations.markings}
\tikzset{midarrow/.style={decoration={markings, mark=at position 0.5 with {\arrow{>}}}, postaction={decorate}}}
\coordinate (S) at (0,1.5);
\coordinate (A) at (2.5,2.7);
\coordinate (B) at (2.5,0.3);
\coordinate (T) at (5.0,1.5);
\draw[midarrow] (S) -- (A) node[midway, above left] {$18$};
\draw[midarrow] (S) -- (B) node[midway, below left] {$22$};
\draw[midarrow] (A) -- (B) node[midway, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$6$};
\draw[midarrow] (A) -- (T) node[midway, above right] {$15$};
\draw[midarrow] (B) -- (T) node[midway, below right] {$17$};
\fill (S) circle (2.5pt) node[left] {$S$};
\fill (A) circle (2.5pt) node[above] {$A$};
\fill (B) circle (2.5pt) node[below] {$B$};
\fill (T) circle (2.5pt) node[right] {$T$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Find the capacity of the cut separating $\{S, A, B\}$ from $\{T\}$, and determine the maximum flow from $S$ to $T$.

